1
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:12,080
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,120
=Episode 14=

3
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,200
So you remember everything.

4
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:18,360
You remember it all, don't you?

5
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,600
Then why were you avoiding me?

6
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:29,840
♪I miss you♪

7
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:30,880
Because of Li Junsheng.

8
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:34,000
If I couldn't eliminate
the threat he posed,

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,080
you'd still be in danger.

10
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,000
So I made up my mind

11
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,960
to stay away from you.

12
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,240
♪Falling for you has become a habit♪

13
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,680
I ignored you again and again.

14
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,320
I kept saying things
I knew would hurt you.

15
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:46,960
And you still put yourself in danger.

16
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:49,000
♪No busy signal can drown them out♪

17
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,600
Do you know how worried I was?

18
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,120
I thought the butterfly effect

19
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,720
made you stop loving me.

20
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,280
But I thought it was okay.

21
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,640
This time around, let me be the one
to protect you.

22
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,520
♪I said goodbye to the carefree me♪

23
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:05,000
How could I ever stop loving you?

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,360
I knew it.

25
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,440
As long as the ring
can still recharge me,

26
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:11,720
that means

27
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,480
our true love is still there.

28
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:16,520
♪And forgot how cold you became♪

29
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:17,640
Recharge you?

30
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:18,240
Yeah.

31
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:21,120
I kept forgetting to tell you this.

32
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:22,680
♪Your greatest charm is all in my head♪

33
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,880
This ring

34
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,360
can replenish my energy.

35
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,440
It's like charging a battery.

36
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,280
When I run out of charge,

37
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:29,520
I get dizzy and lightheaded.

38
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,360
I may even pass out.

39
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,040
Remember last time,
because of Song Shuqi,

40
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,280
I collapsed in the restroom,

41
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,440
ended up in the ER, and nearly died?

42
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,400
It was actually because

43
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:39,560
I needed to recharge.

44
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,040
♪That's why I keep falling♪

45
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,160
So the discipline director's
surprise inspection...

46
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,080
That was your doing too?

47
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,760
♪I thought I could take it all on♪

48
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:51,800
♪I still ended up completely defeated♪

49
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:55,800
Uh...

50
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:01,640
How did you know Li Junsheng
was behind it?

51
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,440
I saw the mask that guy was wearing

52
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:05,440
was exactly like the one Wang Haotian
wore when he kidnapped me.

53
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,560
When I had Wang Haotian
cornered that day,

54
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:09,600
he told me himself

55
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,160
that he and Li Junsheng

56
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,360
had been planning revenge
for a long time.

57
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,720
Wang Haotian showed up that day

58
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:15,840
to lure me away

59
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,960
so the real killer, Li Junsheng,
could go after you.

60
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,440
I always thought Li Junsheng

61
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,120
was acting so humble around me
because he'd realized he was wrong.

62
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:23,800
I never thought...

63
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:24,720
It's okay.

64
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:27,560
This time, we know what he's up to,
and he doesn't know we're aware.

65
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,160
We won't let history repeat itself.

66
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,360
But as for us...

67
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:38,880
we should keep it quiet for now.

68
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:40,840
It might be safer that way.

69
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,600
A secret relationship?

70
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,400
That's kind of exciting.

71
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:47,920
Alright.

72
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:49,840
I should get you home.

73
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,560
As for Li Junsheng,

74
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:52,960
we'll figure out our next move.

75
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:53,960
Okay.

76
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,200
I went to rehab for a routine checkup
today

77
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,480
and made a major breakthrough.

78
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,080
I ran into Wang Haotian.

79
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,720
He's doing rehab at your mom's hospital?

80
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:11,320
Yeah.

81
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,600
Wang Haotian probably

82
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,720
sprained his ankle

83
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,680
when Li Junsheng kicked him
off the wall.

84
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:20,480
I probably ran into him there
in the last loop too.

85
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,200
But back then, I never would've imagined

86
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,200
that he and I would ever be connected.

87
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,360
He Lan,

88
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,560
we can't just let the Li Junsheng
thing go.

89
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:30,680
At the very least,

90
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,760
we can't let Wang Haotian
keep blaming you falsely.

91
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:34,120
Besides,

92
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:36,080
Zhang Jinghang's hand will
be ruined because of this too.

93
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:39,040
This isn't the first time
Li Junsheng has framed me.

94
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,240
Besides, the Wang family
won't believe me.

95
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,520
Whether it was Li Junsheng or me,

96
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,040
they don't care who really did it.

97
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,280
They've already received
a settlement payment.

98
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:50,640
So,

99
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:53,280
Wang Haotian is still our best lead.

100
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:55,760
Maybe

101
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,000
if we talk to him,

102
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,480
we might find a new clue.

103
00:03:58,920 --> 00:03:59,520
At least

104
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,680
we can't let him keep
pinning everything on you.

105
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:04,320
If we go to Wang Haotian now,

106
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,800
I doubt he'll tell us anything.

107
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,280
Then I'll go.

108
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,520
He probably won't be as hostile
toward me.

109
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:11,840
It's too dangerous.

110
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,040
Come on.

111
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:15,760
You're just

112
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:18,560
being overly cautious
after what happened.

113
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,840
Don't forget,

114
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:23,200
Wang Haotian is still just
some teenage kid.

115
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,200
Hmm.

116
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,560
I guess you have a point.

117
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,240
My home's up ahead.

118
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:33,480
Um...

119
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,320
What's wrong?

120
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,280
I need to recharge too.

121
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:39,240
Are you feeling sick too?

122
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:40,280
Well...

123
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,040
I don't need the ring.

124
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:42,720
I...

125
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,280
Xiyu!

126
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:57,040
What are you doing?

127
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:58,840
Did you finish your homework?

128
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,440
I...

129
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,440
was just

130
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:04,760
enjoying the sunset.

131
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,520
I'll be right in.

132
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,040
Hurry up and come home!

133
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,240
Right away!

134
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,480
(Residual Waste)

135
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:57,800
What a coincidence.

136
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,680
You hurt your ankle too?

137
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,240
So did I.

138
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:04,960
I had worse luck, though.

139
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,600
Someone pushed me down the stairs.

140
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,160
You ran into someone bad too?

141
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,240
You did too?

142
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,320
I...

143
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:13,760
got kicked

144
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:14,920
off a wall.

145
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:15,840
He kicked me right off.

146
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,520
What happened?

147
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:19,680
There was this thief.

148
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:21,800
He broke into the raw-material
storage room at my dad's factory.

149
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:22,960
I caught him.

150
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,120
So I chased him.

151
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,640
He tried to escape over a wall,

152
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,560
and I almost caught him.

153
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,560
But to get away from me,

154
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,680
he kicked me

155
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,440
off the wall.

156
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,600
Did they catch him in the end?

157
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,360
Yeah.

158
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:36,880
He paid my family compensation.

159
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,280
Did you...

160
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:40,920
actually see who he was?

161
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,760
I didn't see his face clearly.

162
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,040
But I knew what he was wearing.

163
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,480
Still...

164
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:52,800
he wouldn't admit it.

165
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,480
Too scared to own up to it.

166
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,000
But if all you saw was his clothes,

167
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:58,960
then maybe

168
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,120
it really wasn't him.

169
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,480
Did you notice anything else about him?

170
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,080
Like...

171
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,360
his hairstyle,

172
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,280
or maybe how he smelled?

173
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:09,480
No.

174
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:11,800
Why are you asking?

175
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:15,800
I was just thinking
you're a lot luckier than me.

176
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,800
At least someone covered
your medical bills.

177
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,080
Unlike me.

178
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:20,960
When I got

179
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,840
pushed down the stairs,
everything was so chaotic.

180
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:25,360
I just had to chalk it up to bad luck.

181
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:29,720
Your ankle seems to be
recovering pretty well, though.

182
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,000
It's okay.

183
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,560
I'm the center forward
on our school soccer team.

184
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:36,480
I just don't know

185
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:38,160
if I'll ever be able to play again.

186
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,640
Of course you will.

187
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,280
As long as you keep up with rehab.

188
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,400
But...

189
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,560
I overheard my parents say something
about a Grade 7 disability.

190
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,320
They're keeping it from me,

191
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:49,680
telling me

192
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:50,960
my foot will definitely heal.

193
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,160
When I got hurt,

194
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:58,360
I wondered too

195
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:00,000
if my life was basically over.

196
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,760
But

197
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,240
even if our bodies are injured,

198
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,040
that doesn't make us
any different from anyone else.

199
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,920
Nobody in this world is perfect anyway.

200
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:11,960
Maybe someday soon,

201
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,760
people won't even need bodies anymore.

202
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,600
They'll upload their consciousness

203
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:17,040
into one huge network

204
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,880
connecting the whole world.

205
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,000
And then,

206
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,560
no one will care whether someone's
body is disabled.

207
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:26,440
That's incredible.

208
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:28,960
Sounds like science fiction.

209
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,080
That's gotta be centuries away.

210
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,640
Maybe

211
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:34,320
it's closer than we think.

212
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,480
If that day really comes,

213
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,080
that'd be so cool.

214
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,960
Is that your lighter?

215
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:44,600
You smoke?

216
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:46,080
No.

217
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:46,920
I...

218
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,840
found it at my dad's factory.

219
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,200
No one ever came to claim it,

220
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,280
and I thought it looked cool,

221
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,320
so I kept it.

222
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,480
Can I take a picture of it?

223
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,160
Sure.

224
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:55,880
Thanks.

225
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:00,120
Here.

226
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,440
(I recognize that lighter.)

227
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,840
(It's the keychain for Li Junsheng's
internet cafe key.)

228
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,920
Can we add each other on WeChat?

229
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:15,600
I mean,

230
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,120
we could

231
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,240
share rehab tips and stuff.

232
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,360
I... I don't have a phone yet.

233
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,280
But I have an email address.

234
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:23,600
Email works too.

235
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,280
(This is yours, isn't it?)

236
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,240
(You dropped it)

237
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,600
(when you were stealing
from Wang Haotian's father's factory.)

238
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,440
(So what?)

239
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,720
(The case is already closed.)

240
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,200
(Ever since you came into my family,)

241
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:42,600
(how many times have I taken the blame
for you?)

242
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,160
(This time,)

243
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:46,160
(you have to tell my dad
and your mom the truth.)

244
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:48,320
(What does one keychain prove?)

245
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,480
(Besides, have you ever wondered)

246
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:53,240
(why your dad believes
everything I say about you?)

247
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:54,960
(I'll tell you why.)

248
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,080
(Because you...)

249
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:59,440
(are just a pathetic kid
whose parents never loved him.)

250
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:00,320
(No, wait.)

251
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:01,960
(Not your mom.)

252
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:04,280
(You don't even have one.)

253
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,200
I know Junsheng.

254
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,040
Deep down,

255
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,640
Junsheng's not a bad kid.

256
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:13,000
He's just scared

257
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,840
he'll never measure up to He Lan.

258
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,080
And I brought him

259
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,080
into this family with me.

260
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,760
Of course he's afraid he'll be unwanted.

261
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:19,920
Jianye,

262
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:21,040
I know

263
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,600
He Lan has been treated unfairly.

264
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,480
How about this?

265
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,480
I'll have Junsheng pack his things

266
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:27,200
and stay at my mom's place.

267
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:28,760
He's already a teenage boy.

268
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:31,440
Who'd want to take in
someone else's kid anyway?

269
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:33,960
Don't do that.

270
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:36,720
No one's trying to kick Junsheng out.

271
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:42,920
He Lan,

272
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,560
I'm strict with you

273
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,400
because I'm afraid you'll go down
the wrong path.

274
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:49,320
Ever since your mother passed away,

275
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:51,080
you've changed completely.

276
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:52,760
Dressing strangely,

277
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,960
hanging around the billiards hall
with those punks every day...

278
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,400
I didn't change because Mom died.

279
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,760
I changed after Li Junsheng
and Li Xiaoxia

280
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,120
came into this house.

281
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:02,240
Dad,

282
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,640
those two are not good people.

283
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:05,920
Why do you insist on

284
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,000
wasting your time on them?

285
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:10,720
Jianye,

286
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:11,440
I know

287
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,440
that second marriages aren't easy.

288
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,160
So,

289
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,120
I'll take Junsheng and leave right now.

290
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,360
We'll go find somewhere else to live.

291
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,680
Don't go. Come back!

292
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,920
I know you're disappointed.

293
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:31,400
Once the college entrance exam is over,

294
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,640
you can leave this family behind.

295
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:33,840
Don't worry.

296
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,000
Until then,

297
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:38,120
we just need to stay away
from Li Junsheng.

298
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:38,880
Oh, right.

299
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,480
I already emailed the recording
to Wang Haotian.

300
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,240
I remember Wang Haotian saying

301
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:46,120
he caught Li Junsheng

302
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:47,720
in the raw-material storage room.

303
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:48,960
Yeah.

304
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:51,600
Then something doesn't add up.

305
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,600
If Li Junsheng was stealing money,
why not go to the office?

306
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,560
Why go to the raw-material storage room?

307
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,080
When will this batch be ready?

308
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,320
Someone's already pushing me for it.

309
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:31,280
This formula

310
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,400
has serious side effects.

311
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:33,760
It only suppresses
the disease temporarily.

312
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,200
Long-term use is dangerous.

313
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,520
They all have hepatitis C anyway.

314
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:39,320
They're dying either way.

315
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:41,040
They can't afford the brand-name drugs.

316
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:43,640
They're lucky

317
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,680
they even have our medicine.

318
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:46,840
As for the last batch,

319
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,000
they were just unlucky.

320
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:49,240
Get to work!

321
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:50,320
What are you standing around for?

322
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,160
(Could Li Junsheng be the killer?)

323
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:30,960
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

324
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:37,520
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

325
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,640
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

326
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,800
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

327
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,720
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

328
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:51,200
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

329
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:57,440
♪Through the endless night,
I guard my only secret♪

330
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:04,000
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

331
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,280
♪I tried to erase the fire we once had♪

332
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:11,160
♪But I can't erase your name
carved into my bones♪

333
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:14,000
♪The more I try to leave you behind♪

334
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,120
♪The deeper I sink with no end in sight♪

335
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:21,000
♪What if I stayed a little farther away♪

336
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,400
♪Could I finally break free
from this cycle♪

337
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,800
♪What if I took things a little slower♪

338
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:30,800
♪Could I delay the moment
everything falls apart♪

339
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:34,880
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

340
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,920
♪I could give you another future♪

341
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:44,360
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

342
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:46,680
♪Even if I never want to see you again♪

343
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,320
♪This nightmare still won't end♪

344
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:50,080
♪Even if it all plays out again♪

345
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,360
♪I'll still find my way back to you♪

346
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:56,360
♪Even if having you only leaves me
in your debt♪

347
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,320
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪

348
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:04,080
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪
